# An inference fuse involving a quoted rule
#
# The program contains a rule saying "if Alice is a liar, that is a
# contradiction", and a second rule saying "that first rule itself leads to a
# contradiction". The second rule's premise is a quoted rule, which matches
# the first rule as stated, so it fires and concludes false: an inference
# fuse. Eyeron stops, reports the fired rule and exits with code 65. It shows
# rules whose premise is a quoted rule, and the fuse (=> false).
#
# expect-exit: 65

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/ns#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

# If Alice is a liar, that is a contradiction.
{
    :Alice a :Liar
} => false .

# Having the rule above is itself a contradiction. That rule is in the
# program, so this premise holds and the fuse fires.
{
    {
        :Alice a :Liar
    } => false
} => false .
